.TH DTCPROMETHEUSEXPORTER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
dtcPrometheusExporter \- Prometheus HTTP exporter for Mu2e DTC and CFO register values
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtcPrometheusExporter
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR index ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A single-threaded HTTP/1.x server on
.B INADDR_ANY
(all interfaces), no authentication.
.B GET /metrics
returns the gauge family
.B dtc_register_value
with labels
.BR dtc ,
.BR device_type " (" dtc | cfo ),
.B address
and
.BR register ;
the value is the raw 32-bit register.
Any other path returns 404.
.PP
On every scrape the exporter enumerates
.BI /dev/mu2e N
(or uses
.BR \-d ),
constructs a
.B DTC_Registers
object with
.B skipInit
for each card, and if the design flavour is CFO constructs
.B CFO_Registers
instead.
For a DTC it emits the simple dump, full dump, performance, SERDES-error and
packet-counter register sets; for a CFO the simple dump, full dump and counters.
Each address is emitted once.
Every exception is swallowed: a card that cannot be opened (for example
.B EBUSY
because another UID owns it, see
.BR mu2e (4))
simply disappears from the output with no error metric.
.PP
Because each scrape opens the device, an exporter running as a non-root user
holds ownership of the node for the duration of the scrape; a DAQ process of a
different UID that opens the node in that window gets
.BR EBUSY .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
TCP port.
Default
.BR 9100 ,
which is the conventional
.B node_exporter
port; mu2edaq-operations runs it with
.BR "\-p 9194" .
.TP
.BI \-d " index"
Scrape only this card.
.TP
.BI \-m " file"
Simulator memory file passed to
.B DTC_Registers
(default
.IR mu2esim.bin ).
.TP
.B \-h
Usage, exit 0.
An unknown option prints the usage and exits 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM ;
1 if
.BR socket (2),
.BR bind (2)
or
.BR listen (2)
fails.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE
and
.B CFOLIB_SIM_ENABLE
override hardware mode (see
.BR DTCRegDump (1)).
.SH FILES
.BI /dev/mu2e N
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
dtcPrometheusExporter \-p 9194 &
curl \-s http://localhost:9194/metrics | grep \(aqregister="FPGA Temperature"\(aq
.EE
.PP
The systemd unit in mu2edaq-operations:
.PP
.EX
ExecStart=.../spack\-env/view/bin/dtcPrometheusExporter \-p 9194
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR DTCRegDump (1),
.BR CFORegDump (1),
.BR mu2e (4)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
Manual page written for the September 2026 DAQ mega-review from the source
at commit a5c0ce7.
